---
---

<section class="border-b border-[#232730] bg-[#090a0c] py-20 lg:py-24" id="architecture">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
        Architecture
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
        Reptar couples the type safety and ergonomics of C# with the distributed execution of Cloudflare Workers.
        The TypeScript host shim manages runtime I/O; the compiled Wasm engine executes routing, validation, and domain logic.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Architectural Pipeline Diagram -->
    <div class="mt-12 rounded border border-[#232730] bg-[#0d0e12] p-6 lg:p-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 items-stretch">
        <!-- Stage 1 -->
        <div class="rounded border border-[#232730] bg-[#111317] p-5 flex flex-col justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Tier 1</span>
              <span class="rounded bg-[#1a1d24] px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-zinc-300">Client</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold text-white">Frontend Client</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Consumes <code class="text-zinc-200">createClient&lt;AppType&gt;</code>. Runs in TanStack Start, Expo, Next.js, or curl.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-[#1e232d] font-mono text-[11px] text-emerald-400">
            contracts: JSON / RPC
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stage 2 -->
        <div class="rounded border border-[#232730] bg-[#111317] p-5 flex flex-col justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Tier 2</span>
              <span class="rounded bg-[#1a1d24] px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-zinc-300">Edge Shim</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold text-white">TS Host Shim</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Generated edge worker. Manages cookies, WebCrypto scrypt, telemetry, and Cloudflare environment bindings.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-[#1e232d] font-mono text-[11px] text-emerald-400">
            calls: wasm.handle(...)
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stage 3 -->
        <div class="rounded border border-[#232730] bg-[#161a22] p-5 flex flex-col justify-between border-l-2 border-l-emerald-500">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Core Engine</span>
              <span class="rounded bg-emerald-950/60 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-800">C# Wasm</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold text-white">Reptar Reactor</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
              Compiled via NetWasm. Cached per isolate. Executes routing, middleware, <code class="text-emerald-300">Rule&lt;T&gt;</code> validation, and handlers.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-[#232730] font-mono text-[11px] text-emerald-400">
            imports: db / ai / storage
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Stage 4 -->
        <div class="rounded border border-[#232730] bg-[#111317] p-5 flex flex-col justify-between">
          <div>
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">Tier 4</span>
              <span class="rounded bg-[#1a1d24] px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-zinc-300">Platform</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="mt-3 text-base font-semibold text-white">Cloudflare Edge</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
              Native bindings: D1 relational database, R2 object store, Workers AI inference, and edge rate limiters.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-[#1e232d] font-mono text-[11px] text-emerald-400">
            responses: Typed Envelope
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Lifecycle Detail Table -->
      <div class="mt-8 border-t border-[#232730] pt-6">
        <h4 class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-400 uppercase tracking-wider">
          Request Lifecycle Execution
        </h4>
        <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-xs text-zinc-400">
          <div>
            <span class="font-mono text-white block mb-1">01. Isolate Reuse</span>
            The WebAssembly module is compiled once and kept in worker isolate memory. Cold starts are constrained to initial module load; subsequent requests execute without instantiation overhead.
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="font-mono text-white block mb-1">02. Memory-Mapped Envelope</span>
            Requests cross the JavaScript-Wasm boundary via raw JSON strings. Reptar uses source-generated serialization to eliminate double serialization and avoid runtime reflection.
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="font-mono text-white block mb-1">03. Dual-Target Compilation</span>
            The same C# codebase targets <code class="text-zinc-200">netwasm0.1</code> for Cloudflare Workers and <code class="text-zinc-200">net10.0</code> Native AOT for AWS Lambda and Docker containers.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
